Chapter: MmioGateOpen

 The admitted half of the ARM64 MMIO window gate. It declares Device.Mmio,
 so `a64-emit-boot-grant` puts cap-device in slot 0 of the process table and
 `a64-rt-guarded-access` lets the read through.

 The address is the PL011 flag register on the committed Renode board
 (`tools/renode/codex/codex-arm64.repl`, uart0 at #9000000, FR at offset
 #18). It is read for its ADDRESS, not its value: what this arm proves is
 that a declared program reaches the device at all. The shut arm reads the
 same register from the same instruction and the declaration is the only
 difference between them.

 We say:

Section: Body

  uart-fr : Integer = #9000018

  opening : [Console, Device.Mmio] Nothing = act
    v <- (peek-32 uart-fr 0)
    print-line-uni ("mmio: " & show v)
  end
